// Deep dubstep's bass (docs/design/music.md section 7e, 2026-11-13): the WOBBLE and the SUB in one
// voice. Two detuned saws and a square an octave down through a resonant 24 dB low-pass whose
// cutoff an LFO sweeps in time with the beat, at a rate that changes bar by bar (eighth notes,
// eighth notes, eighth-note triplets, eighth notes: `lfo_rates`), pushed a little into the filter
// and softly saturated after it, half wet (parallel distortion); under it all a clean sine at the
// note, the protected sub, added after every filter and distortion so it stays round, with the
// buzzing part high-passed above it. Each note glides a little from the last. The genre's sidechain
// ducks the whole voice under the kick. All of it the bass toolkit (rung E2), synthesised: for an
// electronic bass that is the genuine article.
Instrument(
    id: "wobble_bass",
    words: "music.instrument.wobble_bass",
    kind: Synth((
        oscillators: [
            (wave: Saw, detune_cents: -7.0),
            (wave: Saw, detune_cents: 7.0),
            (wave: Square, semitones: -12.0, level: 0.5),
        ],
        filter: Some((kind: LowPass, cutoff_hz: 150.0, q: 2.6, key_track: 0.5, lfo_depth_hz: 1500.0, stages: 2, lfo_rates: [2.0, 2.0, 3.0, 2.0], lfo_shape: Sine, drive: 0.25)),
        envelope: (attack_s: 0.006, decay_s: 0.0, sustain: 1.0, release_s: 0.06),
        glide_s: 0.035,
        fx: (
            shaper: Some((curve: Soft, drive: 0.35, mix: 0.6)),
            sub: Some((level: 0.85, octave: 0.0, split_hz: 90.0)),
        ),
    )),
    level_db: -15.5,
    reverb_send: 0.04,
)
